# Trivy ignore file for the Container security workflow.
#
# Each entry is a HIGH/CRITICAL advisory that cannot be resolved by upgrading a
# first-party dependency and does not affect the runtime security of the image.
# Keep this list short and justified; remove entries once an upstream fix ships.

# msgpack is vendored inside pip's private `_vendor` tree (pip/_vendor/msgpack)
# and is used only by pip itself. The application never imports it, and the
# runtime images do not install packages at run time, so it is not reachable.
# No published pip release bundles the fixed msgpack (>=1.2.1) yet.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools PackageIndex path traversal. The application venv ships the fixed
# setuptools (>=78.1.1); the only remaining match is a transient copy pulled in
# by the Playwright browser install layer. The vulnerable code path (using
# setuptools' PackageIndex to download packages) is never invoked at run time.
CVE-2025-47273
